cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite a scenario, cite it by its CAN- identifier and the corpus version
  (e.g. "CAN-CB-012, corpus-v1"); rows are versioned and never silently edited.
title: "Editing Surface Contract"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Electro-Jam Instruments"
abstract: >-
  A cross-editor accessibility conformance corpus and harness for HTML editing
  surfaces: 218 canonical editing operations catalogued from editor source,
  a behavioural contract for what an editing surface must announce, and a
  zero-dependency harness that measures any editor against it headless in CI.
  Measurements are browser-told, not user-heard, and are dated and pinned to
  editor commits.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Electro-Jam-Instruments/Accessible-editor-agen"
license: MIT
version: corpus-v1
date-released: "2026-08-31"
